  "narrative": {
    "intro": "New York has $450M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The state recorded 21,149 awards with an average award size of $21.3K, and obligations fell 96.4% year over year. Fiscal history shows obligations were $32B in FY22, $18.7B in FY23, $17B in FY24, $13.8B in FY25, and $12.7B in FY26. The Department of Veterans Affairs and the Department of Energy are the largest buying agencies so far, with $185M and $154M in obligations respectively. BROOKHAVEN SCIENCE ASSOCIATES LLC is the largest vendor with $154M in obligations. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Biotechnology) is the largest industry by obligations, with $154M. Other notable agencies include the General Services Administration with $43.5M and the Department of Justice with $19.9M. Other vendors with significant obligations include WELCH ALLYN, INC. at $31.1M and BOOZ ALLEN HAMILTON INC at $21.1M.",
    "sections": [
